</div></div></div><div class=3D"index-module--postContent--f670e"><p>I am i=
mpressed by the expressiveness of React hooks. You can do so much by writin=
g so little.</p>
<p>But the brevity of hooks comes at a price =E2=80=94 they're relatively d=
ifficult to understand at the beginning. That's especially true for <code>u=
seEffect()</code> =E2=80=94 the hook that manages side-effects in functiona=
l React components.</p>
<p>I'll help you understand <code>useEffect()</code> in an accessible way. =
Let's get started.</p>
