<ul>
<li><code>callback</code> is a function that contains the side-effect logic=
. <code>callback</code> is executed right after the DOM update.</li>
<li><code>dependencies</code> is an optional array of dependencies. <code>u=
seEffect()</code> executes <code>callback</code> only if the dependencies h=
ave changed between renderings.</li>
</ul>
<p><em>Put your side-effect logic into the <code>callback</code> function, =
then use the <code>dependencies</code> argument to control when you want th=
e side-effect to run. That's the sole purpose of <code>useEffect()</code>.<=
/em></p>
