<p>The <em>document title update</em> is the side-effect because it doesn't=
 directly calculate the component output. That's why the document title upd=
ate is placed in a callback and supplied to <code>useEffect()</code>.</p>
<p>Also, you don't want the document title update to run every time <code>G=
reet</code> component renders. You only want it to happen when the <code>na=
me</code> prop changes =E2=80=94 that's the reason you supplied <code>name<=
/code> as a dependency to <code>useEffect(callback, [name])</code>.</p>
