<p><code>useEffect(callback, [prop, state])</code> invokes the <code>callba=
ck</code> once after mounting, and again after committing the changes to th=
e DOM, <em>if and only if</em> any value in the dependencies array <code>[p=
rop, state]</code> has changed.</p>
<p>By using the dependencies argument of <code>useEffect()</code>, you cont=
rol when the side-effect is called, independently from the rendering cycles=
 of the component. Again, <em>that's the essence of <code>useEffect()</code=
> hook.</em></p>
