le=3D"color: rgb(171, 178, 191);">);</span></span><br></div></div></div></d=
iv></code></div></div>
<p>Cleanup works the following way:</p>
<p>A) After initial rendering, <code>useEffect()</code> invokes the <code>c=
allback</code> with the side-effect. <code>cleanup</code> function is <em>n=
ot invoked</em>.</p>
<p>B) On later renderings, before invoking the next side-effect <code>callb=
ack</code>, <code>useEffect()</code> <em>invokes</em> the <code>cleanup</co=
de> function from the previous side-effect execution (to clean up everythin=
g after the previous side-effect), then invokes the current side-effect.</p=
>
<p>C) Finally, after unmounting the component, <code>useEffect()</code> <em=
>invokes</em> the <code>cleanup</code> function from the latest side-effect=
.</p>
<img src=3D"https://dmitripavlutin.com/d0532a1ba251b6730f64aff0a02b0925/rea=
ct-useeffect-hook-cleanup.svg" alt=3D"React useEffect() hook cleanup">
