<div class=3D"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overf=
low-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=3D"const fetchMethod =3D useC=
allback(async (id) =3D> {
       //  fetching something
}, [id])

useEffect(() =3D> fetchMethod(), [fetchMethod])"><pre class=3D"notranslate"=
><code class=3D"notranslate">const fetchMethod =3D useCallback(async (id) =
=3D&gt; {
       //  fetching something
}, [id])

useEffect(() =3D&gt; fetchMethod(), [fetchMethod])
</code></pre></div>
<p dir=3D"auto">to keep the effect clean and simple. If I have an additiona=
l logic for fetched data(conversion, formatting), should I keep it in the s=
ame useEffect?<br>
Thanks in advance</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto">Here are my considerations:</p>
<ol dir=3D"auto">
<li>I would keep the code simple and skip the use of <code class=3D"notrans=
late">useCallback()</code>. You can put the conversion and formatting logic=
 inside of the useEffect():</li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=3D"useEffect=
(() =3D> {
  const fetchMethod =3D async () =3D> {
    // fetching logic
  };
  fetchMethod();
}, [id])"><pre class=3D"notranslate"><span class=3D"pl-en">useEffect</span>=
<span class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span class=
=3D"pl-kos">)</span> <span class=3D"pl-c1">=3D&gt;</span> <span class=3D"pl=
