          <blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto">Nice article. I am trying to understand is it required to c=
all useEffect() in event handlers (form's onSubmit)</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir=3D"auto">If the request is started when the user submits the form, t=
hen you don't need <code class=3D"notranslate">useEffect()</code>.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">If you need a fetch request on mounting to fill the form wi=
th initial data, then you need <code class=3D"notranslate">useEffect()</cod=
e>.</p>
